{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QM5hXYERA3sewJaLFz19NS","type":"tool_result","content":"go: downloading github.com/google/go-querystring v1.2.0\ngo: downloading modernc.org/libc v1.80.1\ngo: downloading golang.org/x/sys v0.49.0\ngo: downloading github.com/google/uuid v1.6.0\ngo: downloading github.com/dustin/go-humanize v1.1.0\ngo: downloading github.com/mattn/go-isatty v0.0.24\ngo: downloading modernc.org/mathutil v1.7.1\ngo: downloading modernc.org/memory v1.12.1\ngo: downloading github.com/ncruces/go-strftime v1.1.0\ngo: downloading github.com/remyoudompheng/bigfft v0.0.0-20230129092748-24d4a6f8daec\nok  \tgithub.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/servecmd\t0.499s\n5:Finding from reading the code: every per-repo root already goes through `repopath.Join` (`<root>/<owner>/<repo>`, ASCII-lowercased, validated), so no collision is expected and the plan is mainly one proof test plus a lock test. The roots are `state.Dir` (`internal/state/dir.go`), `controller.LockPath` (`internal/controller/lock_unix.go`, suffix `.lock`), `clonePath` (`internal/servecmd/clone.go`, suffix `.git`), `repoWorkDir` (`internal/servecmd/scanners.go`), the local executor's `repoDir(\"work\"|\"logs\")` (`internal/executor/local/layout.go`), and the inline `config` and `roles-repo` roots in `internal/servecmd/serve.go` (the shared-roles cache has landed: `roles-repo`, `SharedDir`). The `.git`/`.lock` suffixes are the only place a collision could arise (`a/b` vs `a/b.git`); they yield `b.git` vs `b.git.git`, which are distinct.\n8:1. New file `internal/servecmd/isolation_test.go` (package `servecmd`, so unexported `clonePath` and `repoWorkDir` are reachable). Add `func repoPaths(home string, repo github.Repo) (map[string]string, error)` (test-only helper) returning one path per root: `state` and `state-dryrun` via `state.Dir(filepath.Join(home,\".ard\"), repo.String(), dryRun)`; `lock` via `controller.LockPath(home, owner, name)`; `clone` via `clonePath`; `work` via `repoWorkDir`; `logs`, `config`, `roles-repo` via `repopath.Join(filepath.Join(home,\".ard\",<kind>), repo.String())`. Use `repopath.Parts` for owner/name. (If `LockPath` is only defined under `//go:build unix`, put the lock parts in a `_unix_test.go` file.)\n9:2. In the same file add `TestRepoPathsDistinct`: a table of pairs that must differ in every root, and also must not be a path prefix of one another: `a-b/c` vs `a/b-c`, `a/b` vs `a/b.git`, `a/b` vs `a/b.lock`, `a/b.git` vs `a/b.git.git`, `a.b/c` vs `a/b.c`, `a_b/c` vs `a/b_c`, `a_b/c` vs `a-b/c`, `a/b_c` vs `a/b-c`, `o/.github` vs `o/github`. Assert no path of repo X equals any path of repo Y across all roots (cross-root comparison too, so e.g. a clone path never equals a work path).\n10:3. Add `TestRepoPathsCaseFold`: `Owner/Repo`, `owner/repo` and `OWNER/REPO` produce identical maps; also `A/B.git` equals `a/b.git`.\n11:4. Add `TestServeLocksPerRepo` (unix build tag): with one `t.TempDir()` as home, acquire `controller.AcquireLeader` for `a/b` and `c/d` (both succeed, release via the returned `Leader`'s release method; check its name in `lock_unix.go`); a second acquisition for `a/b` fails with `errors.Is(err, controller.ErrLeaderHeld)`; one for `A/B` (different case) also fails; after release, it succeeds. Note: flock on the same file from a second open in the same process conflicts, so the test needs no subprocess (the existing `TestLeaderExcludesSecondAndReleases` in `internal/controller/lock_unix_test.go` does the same).\n12:5. Only if a test fails: fix in `internal/repopath/repopath.go` or the offending caller. Any change to existing on-disk layout needs a maintainer decision (migration or fallback lookup); stop and report instead of changing layout silently.\n14:### Test plan\n15:- Command: `go test ./internal/servecmd/ ./internal/repopath/ ./internal/state/ ./internal/controller/` (full: `make test`).\n16:- Cases: `TestRepoPathsDistinct`, `TestRepoPathsCaseFold`, `TestServeLocksPerRepo` as a